@startuml seq-first-login-otp
' =====================================================================
'  SEQUENCE — forgot-password / OTP reset (3-step)
' =====================================================================
title Sequence — Forgot password (OTP reset, 3 steps)

skinparam shadowing false
actor "User (SPA)" as U
participant "gateway :9000" as GW
participant "auth-service :9001" as AUTH
participant "OtpService /\nResetTokenService" as OTP
participant "MailService" as MAIL
participant "KeycloakService" as KS
participant "Keycloak :8081" as KC

== Step 1 — request OTP ==
U -> GW : POST /api/auth/forgot-password { email }
GW -> AUTH : forward (permitAll)
AUTH -> OTP : generate + store OTP (in-memory, ADR-03)
AUTH -> MAIL : email OTP (Gmail App Password)
MAIL --> U : OTP email
AUTH --> U : 200 (OTP sent)

== Step 2 — verify OTP ==
U -> GW : POST /api/auth/verify-otp { email, otp }
GW -> AUTH : forward
AUTH -> OTP : validate OTP → issue reset token
AUTH --> U : 200 { resetToken }

== Step 3 — set new password ==
U -> GW : POST /api/auth/reset-password { resetToken, newPassword }
GW -> AUTH : forward
AUTH -> OTP : validate reset token
AUTH -> KS : resetPassword(user, newPassword)
KS -> KC : Admin REST: set password (not temporary)
KC --> KS : ok
AUTH --> U : 200 (password changed → back to /login)

note over OTP
  OTP / reset-token / first-login / email-verify stores are in-memory today (ADR-03):
  fine for a single instance; swap for Redis before scaling.
end note

@enduml
